   "date": "2017-08-23T08:15:23Z",
   "subject": "Data Entry for breedR + Estimation of GCA and SCA",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font face=\"georgia,serif\" size=\"4\">I have some questions.</font></div><div><font face=\"georgia,serif\" size=\"4\">1. Regarding data input that has to do with families, must data be presented for each individual animal in the family or just a family mean would do?</font></div><div><font face=\"georgia,serif\" size=\"4\">e.g. if I have 56 families comprising 100 individuals each in a half dialel cross involving 4 males and 4 females  (including parental crosses).</font></div><div><font face=\"georgia,serif\" size=\"4\">2. I have compressed my data into a family data set as attached and I want to estimate main genetic effects of Heterosis, Line, GCA and SCA on the traits in the table. I would like to employ the model below:</font></div><div><font face=\"georgia,serif\" size=\"4\"><br></font></div><div>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">Y</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">hijk</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> </span><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">= </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">μ</span></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">a</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">h</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> +</span><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">p</span></i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">1</span></sub><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ii</span></sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">2</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ib</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">2</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">jb</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">3</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ic</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">3</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">jc</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">c</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">2</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ij</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">c</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">3</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ij</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">e</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ijk</span></sub></i></font></font></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">where\r\n<i>Y<sub>hijk</sub></i> is the <i>k<sup>th</sup></i> trait observation on the </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">fi</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">sh population from the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i>\r\nsire and the <i>j<sup>th</sup></i> dam in\r\nthe <i>h<sup>th</sup></i> line crossing (Inter-Hybrid,\r\nIntra-Hybrid or Purebred); </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">μ\r\n</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">is the overall mean; <i>a<sub>h</sub></i> is the effect common to all progeny of the <i>h<sup>th</sup></i> line crossing; <i>p<sub>1ii</sub></i> is the effect common to\r\nall progeny of a mating between the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i>\r\nstrain of sire and the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i>\r\nstrain of dam; <i>g<sub>2ib</sub></i> is the\r\neffect of general combining ability (gca) of the single strain of sire for\r\ninter-hybrids; <i>g<sub>2jb</sub></i> is the\r\neffect of general combining ability of the <i>j<sup>th</sup></i>\r\nstrain of dam among inter-hybrids; <i>g<sub>3ic</sub></i>\r\nis the effect of general combining ability (gca) of the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i> strain of sire for intra-hybrids; <i>g<sub>3jc</sub></i> is the effect of general\r\ncombining ability of the <i>j<sup>th</sup></i>\r\nstrain of dam among intra-hybrids; <i>c<sub>2ij</sub></i>\r\nis the effect of speci</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">fi</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">c\r\ncombining ability (sca) of the <i>ij<sup>th</sup></i>\r\ncross (i </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">= </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">j); and <i>e<sub>ijk</sub></i>\r\nis the random error effect. Subscript 1 denotes that the effects were measured\r\nonly among the progeny of purebred mating, subscript 2 denotes the effects\r\namong the progeny of the inter-hybrid mating and subscript 3 denotes effects among\r\nprogeny of intra-hybrid mating.</span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><br></span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">I have looked at </span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><br></span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><a href=\"https://github.com/famuvie/breedR/wiki/General-and-Specific-Combining-Abilities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/famuvie/breedR/wiki/General-and-Specific-Combining-Abilities&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244753121000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2xT9ZGyd5ysk-VF81Q4xtI\">https://github.com/famuvie/breedR/wiki/General-and-Specific-Combining-Abilities</a> </span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><br></span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">I did understand the mating structure presented but was lost as to what the actual data input should be.</span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">How do I write a code for this data in order to extract main effects as mentioned above and also Least square means attributable to these effects on the traits investigated? </span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">Pardon me if I fail in making some points but with my little experience, I can only try as much.</span></font></font></font></p><p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">I would really appreciate all the suggestions and knowledge in the forum.</span></font></font></font></p>\r\n\r\n<b></b></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "uPlk5howAgAJ",
   "from": "Facundo Muñoz",
   "author": "37c4b6bc71d5d203",
