   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n  \r\n    \r\n  \r\n  <div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\">\r\n    <p>Dear Gabriel,</p>\r\n    <p>the issue with summarising the measurements into family means is\r\n      that it neglects the variation within families (corresponding to\r\n      the residual variance of your model).</p>\r\n    <p>So, either you model family means (by removing the specific\r\n      combining ability term which will be taken into account\r\n      automatically by the residuals) or you model individual\r\n      observations, using the full dataset.</p>\r\n    <p>Hope it helps</p>\r\n    <p>ƒacu.-</p>\r\n    <p><br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <p><br>\r\n    </p>\r\n    <br>\r\n    <div>El 23/08/17 a las 10:15, Gabriel\r\n      Ataguba escribió:<br>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div text=\"#000000\" bgcolor=\"#FFFFFF\"><blockquote type=\"cite\">\r\n      \r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n        <div><font size=\"4\" face=\"georgia,serif\">I have some questions.</font></div>\r\n        <div><font size=\"4\" face=\"georgia,serif\">1. Regarding data input\r\n            that has to do with families, must data be presented for\r\n            each individual animal in the family or just a family mean\r\n            would do?</font></div>\r\n        <div><font size=\"4\" face=\"georgia,serif\">e.g. if I have 56\r\n            families comprising 100 individuals each in a half dialel\r\n            cross involving 4 males and 4 females  (including parental\r\n            crosses).</font></div>\r\n        <div><font size=\"4\" face=\"georgia,serif\">2. I have compressed my\r\n            data into a family data set as attached and I want to\r\n            estimate main genetic effects of Heterosis, Line, GCA and\r\n            SCA on the traits in the table. I would like to employ the\r\n            model below:</font></div>\r\n        <div><font size=\"4\" face=\"georgia,serif\"><br>\r\n          </font></div>\r\n        <div>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px 0px 11px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">Y</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">hijk</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> </span><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">= </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">μ</span></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">a</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">h</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> +</span><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">p</span></i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">1</span></sub><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ii</span></sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">2</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ib</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">2</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">jb</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">3</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ic</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">g</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">3</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">jc</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">c</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">2</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ij</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">c</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">3</span></sub></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ij</span></sub></i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\"> + </span><i><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">e</span></i><i><sub><span style=\"margin:0px;line-height:107%\">ijk</span></sub></i></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">where\r\n                    <i>Y<sub>hijk</sub></i>\r\n                    is the <i>k<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    trait observation on the </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">fi</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">sh population from the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    sire and the <i>j<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    dam in\r\n                    the <i>h<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    line crossing (Inter-Hybrid,\r\n                    Intra-Hybrid or Purebred); </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">μ\r\n                  </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">is the overall mean;\r\n                    <i>a<sub>h</sub></i> is the effect common to\r\n                    all progeny of the <i>h<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    line crossing; <i>p<sub>1ii</sub></i>\r\n                    is the effect common to\r\n                    all progeny of a mating between the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    strain of sire and the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    strain of dam; <i>g<sub>2ib</sub></i>\r\n                    is the\r\n                    effect of general combining ability (gca) of the\r\n                    single strain of sire for\r\n                    inter-hybrids; <i>g<sub>2jb</sub></i>\r\n                    is the\r\n                    effect of general combining ability of the <i>j<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    strain of dam among inter-hybrids; <i>g<sub>3ic</sub></i>\r\n                    is the effect of general combining ability (gca) of\r\n                    the <i>i<sup>th</sup></i> strain of sire for\r\n                    intra-hybrids; <i>g<sub>3jc</sub></i>\r\n                    is the effect of general\r\n                    combining ability of the <i>j<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    strain of dam among intra-hybrids; <i>c<sub>2ij</sub></i>\r\n                    is the effect of speci</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">fi</span><span style=\"margin:0px\">c\r\n                    combining ability (sca) of the <i>ij<sup>th</sup></i>\r\n                    cross (i </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">= </span><span style=\"margin:0px\">j); and <i>e<sub>ijk</sub></i>\r\n                    is the random error effect. Subscript 1 denotes that\r\n                    the effects were measured\r\n                    only among the progeny of purebred mating, subscript\r\n                    2 denotes the effects\r\n                    among the progeny of the inter-hybrid mating and\r\n                    subscript 3 denotes effects among\r\n                    progeny of intra-hybrid mating.</span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><br>\r\n                  </span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">I have looked at </span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><br>\r\n                  </span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><a href=\"https://github.com/famuvie/breedR/wiki/General-and-Specific-Combining-Abilities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/famuvie/breedR/wiki/General-and-Specific-Combining-Abilities&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793244753125000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2KBIn6iSkb0RYbxBnl6sRD\">https://github.com/famuvie/breedR/wiki/General-and-Specific-Combining-Abilities</a> </span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\"><br>\r\n                  </span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">I did understand the mating\r\n                    structure presented but was lost as to what the\r\n                    actual data input should be.</span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">How do I write a code for this\r\n                    data in order to extract main effects as mentioned\r\n                    above and also Least square means attributable to\r\n                    these effects on the traits investigated? </span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">Pardon me if I fail in making\r\n                    some points but with my little experience, I can\r\n                    only try as much.</span></font></font></font></p>\r\n          <p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"georgia,serif\"><font size=\"4\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">I would really appreciate all\r\n                    the suggestions and knowledge in the forum.</span></font></font></font></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n      </div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
